title: "the repo drops direnv and the last git hook"
links:
  - label: "contributor setup"
    href: "https://github.com/indexable-inc/index/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md"
tags:
  - workflow
---

`.envrc` existed to export `core.hooksPath` so git ran the tracked
`.githooks/commit-msg` hook, and to load the flake devShell. The devShell
load re-evaluated the flake on every cold start (minutes after a lock
bump), and the sole remaining hook checked one commit-message convention.
That is a lot of machinery for one regex.

Both are gone: no `.envrc`, no `.githooks/`, nothing to `direnv allow`.
Cloning the repo is the whole setup. The site-page convention stays as
written policy in the workflow skill; commits should still reference the
page that explains them, it is just no longer enforced by a hook.
